{"version":"1.1.0","enabled":true,"name":"Prompt Intent & Scope Review","description":"When a new prompt is submitted, remind the agent to scope the work correctly, align with thesis deliverables, and avoid over-engineering.","when":{"type":"promptSubmit"},"then":{"type":"askAgent","prompt":"Before starting work on this request, apply these principles:\n1. SCOPE: Solve exactly what was asked. Don't add features, abstractions, or defensive code beyond the task.\n2. THESIS ALIGNMENT: Core deliverables are — Account Module, Dashboard, Voice Room (real-time AI feedback on pitch/tone/rhythm/breath), Coaching/Tutorial (structured exercises with AI guidance), Karaoke (sing-along with scoring), Progress Tracking. 'Voice Enhancement' means coaching-driven improvement, NOT audio signal transformation. Target platform is Android only.\n3. CONTRACTS FIRST: If the task involves a new API endpoint or data shape, start with the contract/schema, not the UI.\n4. EXISTING PATTERNS: Match the project's existing patterns — don't introduce new state management, HTTP libraries, or architectural concepts.\n5. SPRINT CONTEXT: Check if this work relates to the current sprint in Sprint.md. If it does, follow the planned checklist.\n6. VALIDATION PLAN: Know how you'll validate before you start writing code (backend: pytest, mobile: dart analyze + build).\n7. BATCH EFFICIENCY: Group related file changes, run validation once at the end, not after every edit."}}